{"availability":"available","full":"sebastian-hanisch/gin-demo","name":"gin-demo","description":"GIN: Summe statt Mittel, Nachbarn zählen - interaktive Streamlit-Demo (numpy von Grund auf)","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T14:06:55Z","updated":"2026-10-04T13:21:47Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sebastianhanisch-gin-demo.streamlit.app/","topics":["demo","german","graph-neural-networks","machine-learning","python","streamlit"],"demo":"https://sebastianhanisch-gin-demo.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.166Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.166Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.166Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.166Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fünftes Stück der Graph-Neural-Network-Linie der \"Konzepte\"-Reihe im Portfolio von Sebastian Hanisch – Operations Research und Machine Learning – Geschwister von graphsage-demo und Nachfolger von gcn-demo (GCN → GraphSAGE, GAT → GATv2, GIN → Graph Transformer; alle sechs Stücke sind gebaut, den Abschluss bildet graph-transformer-demo).","Ein GCN und GraphSAGE mitteln die Nachbarn eines Kunden – und verlieren damit, wie viele es sind: zwei Nachbarn vom Typ A und zehn Nachbarn vom Typ A haben denselben Mittelwert. Ein Graph Isomorphism Network (GIN) (Xu/Hu/Leskovec/Jegelka 2019) summiert stattdessen, $H' = \\mathrm{MLP}\\big((1+\\epsilon)H + AH\\big)$, und rechnet die Summe mit einem kleinen MLP um. Die Demo stellt drei Fragen an dieselbe Nachbarschaft – Anteil (mindestens die Hälfte der Nachbarn vom Typ A), Anzahl (mindestens drei) und Dichte (mindestens sieben Nachbarn, der Typ ist egal) – und misst, welche Aggregation zu welcher…","Bezug zu OR: Kundendichte und die Zahl der Aufträge in der Nähe bestimmen Auslastung und Tourenplanung – Größen, die man zählt, nicht mittelt."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gin-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3870b8bcea840fb71f3e8b80cefab4c79cc20bb386a3a674aa87ace468fd4cb7","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.327Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.327Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Fünftes Stück der Graph-Neural-Network-Linie der \"Konzepte\"-Reihe im Portfolio von Sebastian Hanisch – Operations Research und Machine Learning – Geschwister von graphsage-demo und Nachfolger von gcn-demo (GCN → GraphSAGE, GAT → GATv2, GIN → Graph Transformer; alle sechs Stücke sind gebaut, den Abschluss bildet graph-transformer-demo).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gin-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3870b8bcea840fb71f3e8b80cefab4c79cc20bb386a3a674aa87ace468fd4cb7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gin-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.327Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T13:21:47Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/gin-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.328Z","hash":"3870b8bcea840fb71f3e8b80cefab4c79cc20bb386a3a674aa87ace468fd4cb7","originalBytes":12644,"storedBytes":12644,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["gin","die","mit","und","graphsage","der","mlp","test","mittel","gcn","anteil","ein","ist","summe","von","dichte","eine","gegen","grad","nachbarn","ber","zwei","anzahl","das","ohne","sum","auf","den","kunden","nicht","nur","preset","sind","bei","dem","graph","seed","typ","merkmale","rule","wins","alle","beim","drei","frage","hat","hier","knoten","punkte","raten","regeln","vom","ausdrucksst","density","des","dreiecke","einem","epsilon","gleich","gleiche","gro","kreis","liegt","matrizen","mean","mittlerer","oder","sechs","sich","sie","transformer","unabh","vehikel","vor","vorn","aggregation","aller","count","demo","diese","ein-schicht-perzeptron","every","experiment","feste","gradienten","kein","lauter","mind